        "M050-SRC-AWAY-001::AWAY-C0004-B00131-a2",
        "M050-SRC-AWAY-001::AWAY-C0008-B00248-2"
      ],
      "canonical_claim": "Crossing concentrates complexity in observation and planning, followed by commitment to one whole-party passage and a brief continuous execution with compact resolution. Commitment ends strategic replanning, while execution may still allow immediate spatial responses such as advancing, holding, retreating while possible, protecting another Citizen, releasing cargo, or recovering from separation. Crossing is neither ordinary travel nor turn-based MEET, uses no tactical action-game structure, and may open MEET after severe disruption without itself acquiring turn structure.",
      "human_question": null,
