      ],
      "canonical_claim": "Crossing can impose personal Exposure and other persistent consequences, including delay, wounds, fear, separation, cargo effects, and Tharn, but it does not use MEET's Exposure procedure or Approach strip. Crossing Exposure derives from commitment under pressure, including lane time, load, injury, rescue, failed windows, night speed, fumes, and separation; players see descriptive state and consequences rather than exact hidden numerals.",
